In article <9570@cs.yale.edu> beigel-richard@CS.YALE.EDU (Richard Beigel) writes:
>>goodies, my kitten ran over the trapdoor I dug before.  Sure enough, we
>>both reached the "impossible" piece of code in trap.c, and ended up
>>with a Segmentation Fault:
>Amazing.  Why doesn't the impossible() routine attempt to save?  At least
>the freeinv code saves information so you can rebuild.

Ouch.

The bug happens because although the code takes into account worn items,
leashes are not implemented in the same way as normal worn items.  The bug
will be fixed in patchlevel 7.

The impossible() routine does not attempt to save, but it does not crash the
program either.  All impossible() does is warn you that a sanity check failed.
